## Part three - the boundaries (standing record)

Each exists to stop a specific drift. Do not relax one without replacing what it stops.

| Boundary | Stops |
|---|---|
| Tier derived from `surface` | a second membership list disagreeing with the first |
| Allowlist is authority; schema references | the same component under two names |
| `schema-absent` / `allowlist-absent` checks | two gates silently disagreeing |
| `unknown` is not a count | a broken checker reading as "1 finding" |
| `generatedAt` + staleness | a stale report reading as live |
| Report now; **no verify endpoint** | implying a fix landed when nothing checked |
| **Milvus for matching, Figma for proof** | a similarity score standing in for evidence |
| Audit output outside `dist/` | a build deleting the report |
| A2UI protocol components excluded explicitly | guessing drift from casing |

