## Deferred - decide with the permission model

Not blocked on engineering. Each of these is a permission question, so it waits
until the role/permission layer is settled rather than being guessed now.

1. **How a user binds to their index** - a `default_index` column on `users`, or a
   join table so one user can be granted access to several? The join table is what
   "can also access other indexes" needs if access is per-user rather than open.
2. **What a role may see within an index** - the tier (`primitives` /
   `prompt-composer` / `console`) is the component half; `get_allowed_tags(role)`
   is the permission half. They meet here, so they get decided together.
3. **Whether findings are scoped per-user or per-index** - a finding belongs to the
   index, but two users on one index may have different visible tiers.
